- 39. Final product positioning
  - BodyBrain is the personal memory layer for your physical life.
  - It connects daily activity and fitness with clinical history.
  - It transforms static medical records into an anatomical memory.
  - It preserves doctor discussions and treatment decisions.
  - It shows where documented problems occurred.
  - It remembers how they evolved.
  - It lets the patient carry that context forward.
- 40. Final pitch
  - BodyBrain is a personal AI agent that builds a continuously updated memory of your body. It connects MRI, X-ray, CT, medical reports, doctor discussions, prescriptions, treatments, injuries, symptoms, workouts, Strava activities, and wearable data to an interactive 3D anatomical model and timeline. When a medical record identifies a specific structure, such as a disc, joint, tendon, or nerve, BodyBrain maps that evidence to the corresponding anatomy and keeps the original record attached. Over time, it becomes a living history of what happened to your body, where it happened, what your doctors said, what treatment followed, and how you recovered. When needed, the patient can turn that memory into a structured, source-backed history to share with a doctor.
- 41. Shortest possible pitch
  - BodyBrain remembers your body.
  - From yesterday's workout to an MRI from five years ago, it connects every piece of your physical history to the exact place it belongs.